-- ============================================================================
-- SCHEMA SNAPSHOT — generated from the live production database
-- (lrstswfxfsezdmvkvukc), regenerated 2026-08-03 post-deal-build (deal layer, BOS standalone contract, L9 signature rules, cleanup bundle), replacing migration-chain replay as the
-- test harness's setup path (Task 4, hardening-unit-spec addendum).
--
-- WHY: createTestDb() previously replayed all ~590 migration files in order
-- against a fresh PGlite instance. That chain has a real, load-bearing break
-- (20260709160000_enforce_launch_modules.sql: FK violation on org_modules,
-- because a later migration's seed insert assumes an org row that a fresh
-- replay hasn't created at that point in history) — every test/db/*.test.ts
-- file has therefore never actually run. This snapshot sidesteps the whole
-- class of "migration N assumes migration M's insert already happened with a
-- specific row" bugs by capturing the live database's ACTUAL current state
-- directly, instead of replaying history to reconstruct it.
--
-- ADDITIVE ONLY: no existing migration file is modified, renamed, or deleted.
-- The migration chain still exists, in full, for provenance and for direct
-- production deploys — this snapshot is a second, independent input, used
-- only by the test harness (test/db/harness.ts).
--
-- CONTENTS:
--   1. Full `public` schema — every type, table, function, trigger, index,
--      view, and RLS policy — SCHEMA ONLY (no rows) for every table except
--      the seven named below. `auth`/`storage` are NOT included here; the
--      harness's own BOOTSTRAP block (harness.ts) continues to emulate those
--      minimally, unchanged.
--   2. Seed DATA (rows) for exactly seven tables — pure product configuration,
--      reviewed individually for PII before inclusion, none found:
--        - organizations       (1 row — the tenant: id/name/slug/status only)
--        - service_types       (pure catalog lookup: code/display_name/desc;
--                                added after the first load attempt failed on
--                                contract_templates_service_type_fkey — a real
--                                dependency, not scope creep)
--        - contract_templates
--        - contract_section_defs
--        - contract_clause_defs
--        - contract_field_defs
--        - template_tokens
--      No other table's rows are included. business_config was considered
--      and explicitly EXCLUDED: it carries a real person's name
--      (signatory_name) and a live FK into contacts (signatory_contact_id) —
--      real PII, not anonymous config, despite living in a "config" table.
--
-- DRIFT GUARD: harness.ts's SNAPSHOT_DATA_TABLES set + snapshotDataTargets()
-- assert that no INSERT statement in this file targets a table outside the
-- seven named above; createTestDbFromSnapshot() throws before ever loading
-- the file if that's violated. If a future regeneration of this snapshot
-- picks up rows for an eighth table (e.g. someone re-runs pg_dump with a
-- wider --table list), the harness setup fails loudly instead of silently
-- absorbing whatever that table happens to contain. Changing the allowed
-- table list is a deliberate, reviewed edit to SNAPSHOT_DATA_TABLES in
-- harness.ts — never an accidental side effect of regenerating this file.
-- ============================================================================

